From 3afab32cacb5e2b2208e0aae18a09499c37c1d19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philipp Bogdan <174341097+philippbogdan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 00:16:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] correlation: find groups of data sets down to two
 (significant_clusters.find_small_groups)

OPTICS cannot report a cluster of fewer than min_samples >= 5 data sets, so small groups
(a handful of ligand-bound or differently packed crystals) never appear in the output.
This adds a calibrated detector, run after OPTICS when
significant_clusters.find_small_groups=True:

- counting noise of every pairwise correlation is measured by a bootstrap over
  reflections (Poisson weights, the same draw for all data sets, correlations recomputed
  exactly as cosym computes them); a greedy group scan on the standardised residuals of
  a single-population (rank-1) fit is calibrated against the same scan on the noise
  replicates (significance);
- a group is only reported when its coherence exceeds separation_ratio times that of the
  most coherent subset of the same size inside the populations it is separated from,
  because real sub-populations exist inside one population (cell, hydration);
- groups other than the largest are taken out of the OPTICS clusters.

Tests: tests/algorithms/correlation/test_groups.py.
